## **Step 1: Identify modified pipelines**

Execute the following:

```
cd ~/lma-pipeline-comparison

while IFS= read -r pipeline
do
    if [ "$pipeline" = "beats-squid-logs" ]; then
        echo "$pipeline : ON_HOLD"
        continue
    fi

    if [ ! -f "manual-review-pipelines/$pipeline.conf" ]; then
        echo "$pipeline : FILE_MISSING"
        continue
    fi

    if cmp -s \
        "dev-pipelines/$pipeline.conf" \
        "manual-review-pipelines/$pipeline.conf"
    then
        echo "$pipeline : NO_CHANGE"
    else
        echo "$pipeline : MODIFIED"
    fi

done < manual-review.txt | tee manual-review-results.txt
```

This will classify the pipelines as follows:

| Status         | Meaning                             |
| -------------- | ----------------------------------- |
| `MODIFIED`     | Local configuration has changed     |
| `NO_CHANGE`    | Original DEV configuration retained |
| `ON_HOLD`      | Excluded pending discussion         |
| `FILE_MISSING` | Requires investigation              |

## **Step 2: Copy only the modified pipelines**

After confirming the results from Step 1, execute:

```
while IFS= read -r pipeline
do
    [ "$pipeline" = "beats-squid-logs" ] && continue

    cp -n \
    "manual-review-pipelines/$pipeline.conf" \
    "updated-dev-pipelines/$pipeline.conf"

    echo "Processed: $pipeline"

done < <(awk '$3=="MODIFIED" {print $1}' manual-review-results.txt)
```

The `-n` option prevents overwriting any previously updated configurations.

